Original commit body from 0b43f1891bd46bffd916b62bdf75e573c8508506:

derive_silence_reason stamps `no_candidate_files` -- documented as "the
pass received zero input files ... the only silence the orchestrator can
attribute with certainty" -- whenever AnalysisRun.files_analyzed is 0.
Zero is also the dataclass default, so a linker that read four hundred
files and never assigned the counter was indistinguishable from one that
received no input, and the axis published the confident wrong answer.

Measured on a self-survey by attributing every Path.read_text /
Path.read_bytes to the calling linker module: EIGHT linkers read between
14 and 834 files apiece and were all stamped `no_candidate_files` --
pyffi 389, grpc 397, di-resolution 396, annotation-convention 834,
wasm-bindgen 14, solidity-abi 14, crypto-flow 17, message-dispatch 17.
The statically eligible class is larger than the eight that fired on this
corpus: eighteen linker modules read files and contain no files_analyzed
assignment at all.

Counting moves to the chokepoint rather than into eighteen bodies.
Seventeen linkers assign the counter correctly and eighteen do not, which
is the evidence that "remember to count" does not survive a new linker. A
per-invocation read log in _text_filters is bound by
_run_linker_with_cache -- the one wrapper every linker flows through --
and read_masked_source (36 call sites) now records through it. Two
sibling readers absorb the other 17 direct call sites:
read_source_text (unmasked; annotation_convention's subject IS the
comment region the masker blanks) and read_source_bytes (parser case).
The log is a set of paths, so files_analyzed counts FILES. The stamp is
guarded like duration_ms: a body that assigned the field keeps its value,
because route-handler-linker deliberately stores a route count there.

tests/test_linker_file_read_accounting.py gates the other half: a direct
Path.read_text / Path.read_bytes anywhere in linkers/ fails there, with
_text_filters -- the one module legitimately holding those calls -- as
the positive control, so a detector that stops working cannot masquerade
as a clean result. Stated limit: the gate is syntactic and scoped to
linkers/, and does not check that a body-supplied count is ACCURATE
(websocket-linker reports 2 while reading 405).

Affected passes move from a false `no_candidate_files` to `unreported`,
which means cannot-determine. The truly-silent cohort is therefore larger
than the disclosure showed: 11 pass-runs and 4.21% of pass time, not 3
and 1.9%.

The mypy strict ratchet fired on two bare contextvars.Token annotations
I added (+2 type-arg). I parameterized mine and the two pre-existing ones
beside them: surface 669 -> 667, baseline locked down.

